# Qoder Sonus (`qoder-sonus`) — findings by Qwen 3.8 Max (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: Qoder (`qoder-sonus`; id `qoder/sonus-1.0`; official `qoder.com`)
- Date: 2026-10-30 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **SELF-EXCLUSION (`.md.excluded`).** Qoder Sonus is a **real, distinct, currently-shipping artifact** — Qoder's own built-in model, announced **2026-09-10** across the whole Qoder family (Qoder, Qoder IDE, Qoder CLI, the JetBrains plugin, QoderWake, Cloud Agents), with a clearly-defined specialty (**Computer Use / desktop-and-pro-software automation, marathon-length autonomous tasks, coding, financial modelling**). **However, it has ZERO verified public capability benchmarks** — no independent measurement (Artificial Analysis has **no page for it — 404**; no Vals, OSWorld, SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench or LMArena figure exists), and **no vendor-published numbers** either: Qoder's own announcement and X post are **entirely qualitative** ("built for marathon-length autonomous tasks, the hardest knowledge work, and serious coding … at its best when using your computer"), and the only quantities in circulation are **pricing/usage** (a **3.2x→8x Qoder-Credits multiplier**, "4,000 daily credits" promo, users reporting runaway credit burn), **not capability**. Scoring Reasoning / Coding / Tool-use would therefore require **inventing benchmark numbers**, which the research rules forbid. This is the same basis on which I self-excluded **longcat-2.5-preview** ("real API-only artifact but zero verified benchmarks of its own") and **fledge-alpha**. Excluded — unscorable without fabrication, not because the model is fake.

## Model card (real artifact — zero verified benchmarks)

- **Name:** Qoder Sonus (/ˈsoʊnəs/) — vendor **Qoder** (the AI-coding IDE family); its **own built-in model**, not a re-hosted third-party SKU.
- **Short description (vendor):** "built for marathon-length autonomous tasks, the hardest knowledge work, and serious coding — and it's at its best when using your computer." Paired with **Computer Use** (Qoder Desktop 0.2.3), it "drives your machine and pro software directly: writing code, building financial models, running research, producing spreadsheets."
- **Provider / access:** Built into the Qoder family (IDE / CLI / JetBrains plugin / QoderWake / Cloud Agents). **Priced in Qoder Credits**, multiplier **3.2x at launch** (personal + enterprise), later reported at **8x**; a "Limited-Time SOTA" promo granted 4,000 daily credits (Sept 21–25). **No per-token API price** — so no AA cost/speed measurement is possible.
- **Release / knowledge:** **2026-09-10** (Qoder forum announcement + Qoder on X). **Current.**
- **IDs:** `qoder/sonus-1.0`; official `qoder.com` / `forum.qoder.com` / `docs.qoder.com`.
- **Context window:** **Not published** for Sonus (the Qoder Model Selector exposes an adjustable Context parameter, but no fixed figure is stated).
- **Modalities:** Curated meta says **"Text in/out,"** but the **Computer Use** specialty means **page/window/screenshot content enters the Agent context** (per `docs.qoder.com/qoder/computer-use`) — i.e. it is effectively **screen/vision-driven for GUI control**. Unverified which modalities are native to Sonus itself.
- **Architecture:** **Undisclosed.** Qoder does not publish parameters, training, or whether Sonus is trained in-house or a fine-tune/route of another frontier model.

### Raw benchmarks found

**None.** No independent harness lists Qoder Sonus (AA 404; absent from Vals, OSWorld/OSWorld-2.0, SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, LMArena). No vendor benchmark table exists — Qoder's announcement, X post and docs give **only qualitative capability claims and credit-multiplier pricing**. Third-party mentions (relayhall.com "Harness Atlas," unifuncs ZCode-vs-Qoder comparison, Reddit r/ClaudeAI) describe Sonus as a **computer-use harness/native model** but cite **no scores**. The curated meta's "SOTA rate applies" refers to the **credit rate**, not a benchmark.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Omitted — self-excluded (real distinct artifact, but **zero verified public capability benchmarks**; assigning Tool-use / Reasoning / Coding scores would require inventing numbers).

